# aql — working todo

Scratch list. The structured version is ROADMAP.md; this is the running one.

## direction (see ARCHITECTURE.md)
- Aql = one hub that owns everything physical. Seven device kinds: camera, lighting,
  robot, climate, energy, sensor, access. Access is the ONE that's real end to end —
  the first module, not the product.
- Chat is an input surface across the hub, not the product. Gates are today's working
  instance because they're the only device class there is to command.
- Shipped: the hub (open path, console, audit, SQLite), the controller agent
  (pinned-key pairing, fail-closed verification, offline LAN grants), signed commands,
  proto/'s 61 vectors / 68 checks, the e2e harnesses.
- Not shipped: the device engine, automations, energy, the camera pipeline, the phone
  half of offline grants. Six of the seven kinds are demo data (`src/lib/demoData.ts`).

## naming, settled
- The hub is a **hub**. Never "the gateway" in prose — in the KOTVA family that word is
  the legacy-rail coordinator role, which is Ephor's job. `gateway/`, the Go module path,
  the binary name, `LINTEL_*`, `lintel.db`, `_lintel._tcp` and proto/vectors/ all keep
  their spelling: compat surface.

## next up
- [ ] app-side offline grants: request / store / refresh, then present over LAN + BLE.
      Three of four pieces already exist (contract, controller verification, hub
      issuance) — this closes the loop. Needs an emergency screen in src/.
- [ ] GPIO relay driver behind `-tags gpio` (today: a stub that panics; default build
      logs). Fail-safe spec: normally-open, line drops on exit/panic.
- [ ] BLE radio validation on real Linux/BlueZ hardware — framing + session are tested,
      the radio has never run. No peripheral backing exists off Linux at all.
- [ ] decide where the device engine lives: Go hub vs the Rust core in src-tauri/.
      Hub is the likely answer (owns persistence, audit, the always-on box). Write it
      down in ARCHITECTURE.md §8 once decided.
- [ ] first driver behind the seam — MQTT is the cheapest breadth (and the likely Zana
      transport).
- [ ] bring access onto the same internal device model once that model exists, so it is
      one kind among seven rather than a parallel stack.

## chat rail → Ephor (in progress)
- [ ] the WhatsApp / Slack / Telegram adapters move OUT of Aql and into Ephor
      (github.com/vul-os/ephor). Target shape: Ephor terminates the rail and hands the hub
      an authorised command; the hub checks rules, signs, actuates. Swappable — run one or
      point at one.
- [ ] `gateway/internal/channels/` is transitional until that lands. Don't document it as
      the supported path; don't rip it out either — it's what works today.
- [ ] `scripts/feature-claims.manifest.mjs` still has `whatsapp-channel`, `slack-channel`,
      `telegram-channel`, `slack-socket-mode` as shipped Aql claims. The code IS still
      there, so those entries are truthful today — revisit when the move lands rather
      than weakening them now.
- [ ] Telegram long-polling (`getUpdates`) — the zero-ingress path for that channel.
      Probably lands in Ephor rather than here.
- [ ] Discord — designed into the seam, no code yet. Same question: whose seam?
- [ ] extend the intent vocabulary past `open`/`close` once there is more than one device
      class to command
- [ ] DMTAP channel stays a scaffold with a fail-closed transport until there is a real
      wire format. Do not present it as a channel.

## console ↔ hub drift (tracked by src/lib/__tests__/routeParity.test.ts)
Each of these is UI with no backend. Either build the route or remove the screen.
- [ ] analytics: `/analytics/accounts/{id}/summary|insights`, `/analytics/locations/{id}/summary`
- [ ] per-access-point maintenance log (`GET/POST /access-points/{id}/maintenance`)
- [ ] password reset / email verify / update password / Google OAuth
- [ ] `/reference/countries`, `/phones/me/phones`, `PUT /auth/me/slack`, `PATCH /auth/me/profile`

## api & integrations
- [ ] scoped API tokens (`aql_live_…`), issued per location, read / read-write
- [ ] outbound webhooks (`open.succeeded`, `open.denied`, `device.offline`,
      `member.revoked`) with HMAC-signed delivery
- [ ] a token-scoped `GET /v1/events` feed (today the audit log is instance-admin only)
- [ ] revoke-a-controller endpoint (no DELETE on /v1/devices yet)
- [ ] API docs with python/go/curl examples

## security / ops
- [ ] 2FA, and some in-band recovery for a lost sole instance-admin password
- [ ] grant revocation beyond "wait for the TTL" (accepted v0 non-goal today)
- [ ] OS-keychain credential vault for device/service secrets — ROADMAP Phase 2. Today
      there is no keychain/keyring code at all, and the hub's signing key + JWT secret sit
      unencrypted in the data directory
- [ ] controller position/tamper sensors return static values — wire real ones
- [ ] pen test the pairing + signed-command path against the proto vectors
- [ ] publish the aql-gateway image automatically (docker.yml is workflow_dispatch only)

## hygiene
- [ ] `.env.example` still documents a `backend/` directory that no longer exists and a
      Postgres `DATABASE_URL` nothing reads
- [ ] `src/mocks/*` is dead code — nothing imports it (the screenshotter uses
      `scripts/screenshotter-fixtures/`). Delete or wire it up.
- [ ] `assets/brand/lintel-*.svg` are stale; `aql-mark.svg` exists alongside
- [ ] `assets/screens/*.png` predate the fold — they picture the retired SvelteKit shell.
      Regenerate against the real console or delete them.
- [ ] `src-tauri`'s `system_pulse` IPC command is never called by the frontend
- [ ] stale `backend/` references in load-bearing code comments
      (`gateway/internal/httpapi/server.go`, `src/lib/api.ts`, `routeParity.test.ts`)
- [ ] test the WhatsApp flow end to end at a real gate: multi-access-point picker,
      location-first flow, "hi" fallback lists linked locations or says not linked

## do not resurrect (removed by decision)
- billing / wallet / subscriptions / invoices / VAT / referrals / payouts / pricing tiers
  — Aql has NO billing system. Operators solve money outside the system; see
  ARCHITECTURE.md §4 "Money is out of scope".
- the Cloudflare Workers + Postgres backend. Deleted. The Go hub is the only server.
- the SvelteKit shell itself. The fold replaced it with the React console; its demo
  dataset was ported over verbatim and is still the source for six of the seven kinds.
- renaming `LINTEL_*`, `lintel.db` or `_lintel._tcp`. Deployment and wire contract for
  hardware already in the field.
